From: Dylan Tisdall <mtisdall@pennmedicine.upenn.edu>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:11:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] adapt: opt-in vertex lock (AdaptOpts::lock_tag)

AdaptOpts::lock_tag names an I8 tag with one component on every
dimension. When it is set, no edge collapse removes a vertex whose tag
value is nonzero. The check is applied with check_collapse_class in
coarsen_element_based1, so it covers coarsen_by_size, coarsen_slivers
and coarsen_verts. The option is off by default (empty name).

Refinement, swaps and collapses do not move existing vertices, so a
locked vertex keeps its exact coordinates. The tag must be transferred
with OMEGA_H_INHERIT (checked in validate()). A split point inherits the
value of the split edge, and an edge cut across a face inherits the
value of the face, so the EDGE and FACE values choose whether new
boundary vertices are locked too.

unit_lock adapts a box with a locked boundary and checks that every
locked vertex stays at identical coordinates, that the boundary is only
subdivided, and that a control run without the lock does remove
boundary vertices.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
